HR Analytics Dashboard
Employee Workforce & Attrition Analysis

Prepared by: Shivani Jogi
Tools: Python | SQL | Excel | Power BI

1. Executive Summary

This project presents an end-to-end HR Analytics solution designed to analyze employee workforce data and identify patterns related to employee attrition, salary, demographics, departments, job roles, and employee tenure.

The project uses Python, SQL, Excel, and Power BI to transform raw employee data into meaningful business insights.

An interactive Power BI dashboard was developed to help HR teams monitor important workforce KPIs, compare employee groups, analyze attrition patterns, and drill down into employee-level details.

2. Business Problem

Employee attrition is an important challenge for organizations because high employee turnover can increase recruitment costs, reduce productivity, affect team performance, and create workforce instability.

HR teams often have large amounts of employee data but may not have an effective way to analyze this information and identify important workforce patterns.

The organization needs a data-driven solution to answer questions such as:

How many employees are currently in the organization?
What is the overall employee attrition rate?
Which departments have higher attrition?
Which job roles experience greater employee turnover?
How is the workforce distributed by gender and education?
How does salary vary across departments and job roles?
How does employee tenure relate to attrition?
Which employee groups require further HR investigation?

The purpose of this project is to convert employee data into clear, interactive, and actionable HR insights.

3. Business Objectives

The main objectives of the project are:

Analyze the overall employee workforce.
Measure employee attrition and attrition rate.
Identify departments with higher attrition.
Analyze employee distribution by gender.
Analyze education and job-role distribution.
Understand salary patterns across the organization.
Analyze employee tenure and years at company.
Identify workforce groups that may require further investigation.
Build an interactive HR Analytics Dashboard.
Provide data-driven recommendations for HR decision-making.
4. Dataset Description

The project uses an employee-level HR dataset containing information about employees, demographics, education, departments, job roles, salary, years at the company, and attrition status.

Dataset Information
Category	Examples
Employee Information	Employee ID
Demographics	Age, Gender
Education	Education Level
Organization	Department
Job Information	Job Role
Compensation	Salary
Experience	Years at Company
Employee Status	Attrition

Total Records: 5,000 employees

